<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Canton of Säntis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a>–<a href="/years/1803">1803</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a> of Säntis was an administrative unit of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a> from 1798 to 1803, named after the Säntis mountain. It combined Appenzell, the city and abbey lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a>, the Toggenburg and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> valley, with St. Gallen as its capital. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-mediation">Act of Mediation</a> of 1803 dissolved it, restoring Appenzell and creating the Canton of St. Gallen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canton-of-santis.jpg" alt="Canton of Säntis" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kantone_Linth_und_Saentis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
